"Object methods follow the same argument-count rule as named functions."
calculator is object
    add is function takes left as number, right as number giving number
        return left + right
    multiply is function takes left as number, right as number giving number
        return left * right

print calculator.add 2, 3
results is calculator.add 2, 3, calculator.multiply 4, 5
print results

"An alias refers to the same object."
alias is calculator
print alias.multiply 3, 7

"Like copies the properties into another object."
copy is object like calculator
copy.add is function takes left as number, right as number giving number
    return left + right + 100
print copy.add 2, 3
print calculator.add 2, 3

"A comma after the method's arguments starts the next array element."
print calculator.add 2, 3, 9
